---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro'
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro'
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Why PrismaLens exists and the rules it is built on.">
  <Hero
    title="About PrismaLens"
    subtitle="Most of an incident is finding the cause. PrismaLens gives that part to a coding agent and keeps the evidence where you can check it."
  />
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="space-y-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-foreground">Why it exists</h2>

      <p>
        When an alert fires, the dashboards usually already hold the answer. The slow part is
        connecting them: which deploy, which change, which line of code. Coding agents have
        become good at reading a codebase and following a trail, and most engineers already
        have one installed and signed in.
      </p>

      <p>
        PrismaLens puts that agent to work on the incident. It opens the incident from the
        alert, gives the agent a read-only copy of the service's code, refuses anything that
        would change it, and keeps the whole run: the report, the evidence and every command
        the agent ran.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-8">What it is built on</h3>

      <p>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Evidence over scores.</strong> A report ranks hypotheses
        and shows what each one rests on. It never prints a confidence percentage, because a
        number you cannot check is worse than none.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Your agent, your login.</strong> PrismaLens never calls a
        model and never reads your agent's credentials. There is no PrismaLens account and
        nothing to pay us.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Say where the limits are.</strong> The read-only policy is
        a guardrail, not a wall, and the docs say so. Every report states whether the run was
        sandboxed.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong class="text-foreground">Yours to run.</strong> PrismaLens is open source
        (Apache-2.0) and runs on your machine. Everything it keeps is in one folder,
        <code>~/.prismalens</code>, and nothing is sent to us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CTA
    title="Join the community"
    description="Star the repo, open an issue with feedback or bug reports, or just say hello. Code contributions open up a little later."
    href="https://github.com/prismalens/prismalens"
    label="View on GitHub"
  />
</BaseLayout>
